ernel’s IP framework for transforming packets (XFRM subsystem). This issue may allow a malicious user with CAP_NET_ADMIN privileges to cause a 4 byte out-of-bounds read of XFRMA_MTIMER_THRESH when parsing netlink attributes, leading to potential leakage of sensitive heap data to userspace.","score":4.4,"severity":"MEDIUM","cvss_version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:N","cvss_source":"nvd@nist.gov","cwe":["CWE-125"],"products":["redhat:enterprise linux","fedoraproject:fedora","linux:linux kernel","debian:debian linux"],"refs":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:6583","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-3773","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2218944","tags":["Issue Tracking","Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2023/10/msg00027.html","tags":[]},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2023/dsa-5492","tags":[]},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/html/ssa-794697.html","tags":[]}],"origin":"nvd","kev":0,"kev_added":"","ransomware":0,"epss":0.00251,"epss_pct":0.1671},{"id":"CVE-2023-3745","published":"2023-07-24T16:15:13","modified":"2026-11-07T12:17:32","status":"Modified","source":"secalert@redhat.com","desc":"A heap-based buffer overflow issue was found in ImageMagick's PushCharPixel() function in quantum-private.h. This issue may allow a local attacker to trick the user into opening a specially crafted file, triggering an out-of-bounds read error and allowing an application to crash, resulting in a denial of service.","score":5.5,"severity":"MEDIUM","cvss_version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","cvss_source":"nvd@nist.gov","cwe":["CWE-125","CWE-787"],"products":["imagemagick:imagemagick"],"refs":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-3745","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2223557","tags"