ied","source":"secalert@redhat.com","desc":"An out-of-bounds memory access flaw was found in the Linux kernel’s TUN/TAP device driver functionality in how a user generates a malicious (too big) networking packet when napi frags is enabled. This flaw allows a local user to crash or potentially escalate their privileges on the system.","score":7.8,"severity":"HIGH","cvss_version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","cvss_source":"nvd@nist.gov","cwe":["CWE-787","CWE-416"],"products":["linux:linux kernel","redhat:enterprise linux"],"refs":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:6799","tags":["Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:6813","tags":["Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7370","tags":["Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7379","tags":["Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7382","tags":["Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7389","tags":["Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7411","tags":["Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7418","tags":["Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7548","tags":["Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7549","tags":["Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]}],"origin":"nvd","kev":0,"kev_added":"","ransomware":0,"epss":0.00344,"epss_pct":0.2811},{"id":"CVE-2023-3019","published":"2023-07-24T16:15:12","modified":"2026-11-07T12:17:30","status":"Modified","source":"secalert@redhat.com","desc":"A DMA reentrancy issue leading to a use-after-free error was found in the e1000e NIC emulation code in QEMU. This issue could allow a privileged guest user to crash the QEMU process on the host, resulting in a denial of service.","score":6.5,"severity":"MEDIUM","cvss_version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:N/A:H","cvss_source":"nvd@nist.gov","cwe":["CWE-416"],"products":["qemu:qemu","redhat:enterprise linux"],"refs":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0135","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0404","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0569","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:2135","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-3019","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2222351","tags":["Issue Tracking","Patch","Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2025/04/msg00042.html","tags":[]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20230831-0005/","tags":[]},{"url":"https://cert-portal.siemens.com/productcert/html/ssa-577017.html","tags":[]}],"origin":"nvd","kev":0,"kev_added":"","ransomware":0,"epss":0.00318,"epss_pct":0.2485},{"id":"CVE-2023-3567","published":"2023-07-24T16:15:12","modified":"2026-11-07T12:17:31","status":"Modified","source":"secalert@redhat.com","desc":"A use-after-free flaw was found in vcs_read in drivers/tty/vt/vc_screen.c in vc_screen in the Linux Kernel. This issue may allow an attacker with local user access to cause a system crash or leak internal kernel information.","score":7.1,"severity":"HIGH","cvss_version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H","cvss_source":"nvd@nist.gov","cwe":["CWE-416"],"products":["linux:linux kernel","redhat:enterprise linux","canonical:ubuntu linux"],"refs":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0412","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0431","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0432","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0439","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0448","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0575","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:2394","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:2950","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:3138","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-3567","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]}],"origin":"nvd","kev":0,"kev_added":"","ransomware":0,"epss":0.00419,"epss_pct":0.3648},{"id":"CVE-2023-33951","published":"2023-07-24T16:15:11","modified":"2026-11-06T21:17:00","status":"Modified","source":"secalert@redhat.com","desc":"A race condition vulnerability was found in the vmwgfx driver in the Linux kernel. The flaw exists within the handling of GEM objects. The issue results from improper locking when performing operations on an object. This flaw allows a local privileged user to disclose information in the context of the kernel.","score":5.3,"severity":"MEDIUM","cvss_version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N","cvss_source":"nvd@nist.gov","cwe":["CWE-413","CWE-362","CWE-667"],"products":["linux:linux kernel","redhat:enterprise linux","redhat:enterprise linux for real time","redhat:enterprise linux for real time for nfv"],"refs":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:6583","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:6901","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7077","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:1404","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:4823","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:4831","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-33951","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2218195","tags":["Issue Tracking","Patch"]},{"url":"https://www.zerodayinitiative.com/advisories/ZDI-CAN-20110/","tags":["Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]}],"origin":"nvd","desc_es":"Se encontró una vulnerabilidad de condición de ejecución en el controlador vmwgfx del kernel de Linux. El fallo existe en el manejo de objetos GEM. El problema se debe a un bloqueo inadecuado al realizar operaciones en un objeto. Este fallo permite que un usuario local privilegiado revele información en el contexto del kernel.","kev":0,"kev_added":"","ransomware":0,"epss":0.00343,"epss_pct":0.2804},{"id":"CVE-2023-33952","published":"2023-07-24T16:15:11","modified":"2026-11-06T21:17:00","status":"Modified","source":"secalert@redhat.com","desc":"A double-free vulnerability was found in handling vmw_buffer_object objects in the vmwgfx driver in the Linux kernel. This issue occurs due to the lack of validating the existence of an object prior to performing further free operations on the object, which may allow a local privileged user to escalate privileges and execute code in the context of the kernel.","score":6.7,"severity":"MEDIUM","cvss_version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H","cvss_source":"nvd@nist.gov","cwe":["CWE-415"],"products":["linux:linux kernel","redhat:enterprise linux","redhat:enterprise linux for real time","redhat:enterprise linux for real time for nfv"],"refs":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:6583","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:6901","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7077","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:1404","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:4823","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:4831","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-33952","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2218212","tags":["Issue Tracking","Patch","Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://www.zerodayinitiative.com/advisories/ZDI-CAN-20292","tags":["Patch","Third Party Advisory","VDB Entry"]}],"origin":"nvd","desc_es":"Se encontró una vulnerabilidad de double free en el manejo de objetos vmw_buffer_object en el controlador vmwgfx en el kernel de Linux. Este problema se produce debido a la falta de validación de la existencia de un objeto antes de realizar más operaciones libres en el objeto, lo que puede permitir a un usuario privilegiado local escalar privilegios y ejecutar código en el contexto del kernel.","kev":0,"kev_added":"","ransomware":0,"epss":0.00465,"epss_pct":0.4051},{"id":"CVE-2022-2127","published":"2023-07-20T15:15:11","modified":"2026-11-05T09:17:04","status":"Modified","source":"secalert@redhat.com","desc":"An out-of-bounds read vulnerability was found in Samba due to insufficient length checks in winbindd_pam_auth_crap.c. When performing NTLM authentication, the client replies to cryptographic challenges back to the server. These replies have variable lengths, and Winbind fails to check the lan manager response length. When Winbind is used for NTLM authentication, a maliciously crafted request can trigger an out-of-bounds read in Winbind, possibly resulting in a crash.","score":5.9,"severity":"MEDIUM","cvss_version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","cvss_source":"nvd@nist.gov","cwe":["CWE-125"],"products":["samba:samba","redhat:enterprise linux","fedoraproject:fedora","debian:debian linux"],"refs":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:6667","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7139","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0423","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0580","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2022-2127","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2222791","tags":["Issue Tracking","Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://www.samba.org/samba/security/CVE-2022-2127.html","tags":["Mitigation","Vendor Advisory"]},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2024/04/msg00015.html","tags":[]},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce@lists.fedoraproject.org/message/BPCSGND7LO467AJGR5DYBGZLTCGTOBCC/","tags":[]},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce@lists.fedoraproject.org/message/OT74M42E6C36W7PQVY3OS4ZM7DVYB64Z/","tags":[]}],"origin":"nvd","kev":0,"kev_added":"","ransomware":0,"epss":0.01722,"epss_pct":0.7763},{"id":"CVE-2023-34967","published":"2023-07-20T15:15:11","modified":"2026-11-06T21:17:00","status":"Modified","source":"secalert@redhat.com","desc":"A Type Confusion vulnerability was found in Samba's mdssvc RPC service for Spotlight. When parsing Spotlight mdssvc RPC packets, one encoded data structure is a key-value style dictionary where the keys are character strings, and the values can be any of the supported types in the mdssvc protocol. Due to a lack of type checking in callers of the dalloc_value_for_key() function, which returns the object associated with a key, a caller may trigger a crash in talloc_get_size() when talloc detects that the passed-in pointer is not a valid talloc pointer. With an RPC worker process shared among multiple client connections, a malicious client or attacker can trigger a process crash in a shared RPC mdssvc worker process, affecting all other clients this worker serves.","score":5.3,"severity":"MEDIUM","cvss_version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L","cvss_source":"nvd@nist.gov","cwe":["CWE-843"],"products":["samba:samba","fedoraproject:fedora","redhat:enterprise linux","debian:debian linux"],"refs":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:6667","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7139","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0423","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0580","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-34967","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2222794","tags":["Issue Tracking"]},{"url":"https://www.samba.org/samba/security/CVE-2023-34967.html","tags":["Vendor Advisory"]},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce@lists.fedoraproject.org/message/BPCSGND7LO467AJGR5DYBGZLTCGTOBCC/","tags":[]},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce@lists.fedoraproject.org/message/OT74M42E6C36W7PQVY3OS4ZM7DVYB64Z/","tags":[]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20230731-0010/","tags":[]}],"origin":"nvd","kev":0,"kev_added":"","ransomware":0,"epss":0.61199,"epss_pct":0.9917},{"id":"CVE-2023-34968","published":"2023-07-20T15:15:11","modified":"2026-11-06T21:17:01","status":"Modified","source":"secalert@redhat.com","desc":"A path disclosure vulnerability was found in Samba. As part of the Spotlight protocol, Samba discloses the server-side absolute path of shares, files, and directories in the results for search queries. This flaw allows a malicious client or an attacker with a targeted RPC request to view the information that is part of the disclosed path.","score":5.3,"severity":"MEDIUM","cvss_version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N","cvss_source":"nvd@nist.gov","cwe":["CWE-201"],"products":["samba:samba","fedoraproject:fedora","redhat:storage","redhat:enterprise linux","debian:debian linux"],"refs":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:6667","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7139","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0423","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0580","tags":[]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2023-34968","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2222795","tags":["Issue Tracking","Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://www.samba.org/samba/security/CVE-2023-34968.html","tags":["Vendor Advisory"]},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce@lists.fedoraproject.org/message/BPCSGND7LO467AJGR5DYBGZLTCGTOBCC/","tags":[]},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce@lists.fedoraproject.org/message/OT74M42E6C36W7PQVY3OS4ZM7DVYB64Z/","tags":[]},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20230731-0010/","tags":[]}],"origin":"nvd","kev":0,"kev_added":"","ransomware":0,"epss":0.01333,"epss_pct":0.7131},{"id":"CVE-2023-34966","published":"2023-07-20T15:15:11","modified":"2026-11-07T07:16:59","status":"Modified","source":"secalert@redhat.com","desc":"An infinite loop vulnerability was found in Samba's mdssvc RPC service for Spotlight. When parsing Spotlight mdssvc RPC packets sent by the client, the core unmarshalling function sl_unpack_loop() did not validate a field in the network packet that contains the count of elements in an array-like structure. By passing 0 as the count value, the attacked function will run in an endless loop consuming 100% CPU. This flaw allows an attacker to issue a malformed RPC request, triggering an infinite loop, resulting in a denial of service condition.","score":7.5,"severity":"HIGH","cvss_version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H","cvss_source":"nvd@nist.gov","cwe":["CWE-835"],"products":["samba:samba","fedoraproject:fedora","redhat:enterprise linux","debian:debian linux"],"refs":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:6667","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2023:7139","tags":["Third Party Advisory"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2024:0423","tags":[]},{"url":"https